{
  "id": "ss.enemy.tryst",
  "name": "Tryst",
  "description": "The flats' last arrival, 색세기, drawn side-on like every other flyer: a lovebug. Black abdomen with a violet sheen so it holds against dark ground, the red-orange scutum over a black underside that is the species' one mark, a black head with a small high eye, a stub of antenna, the hive's organ underneath where abdomen meets thorax. Two-joint wings like the Flitter's, pale so they carry the read, the far pair darker behind. No legs worth the name: two tucked nubs, because a flyer's legs on show read as a spider. She is the largest of the three that arrive together and the one left at the end. Clips: `fly` (the buzz, roots leading tips), `spray` (the abdomen flicks up and the organ flares as the three fling acid in a spin), `flap` (enraged: whole-arm strokes; `meta.flapCue` is the downbeat, when the game surges her), `death` (wings drop onto the back, the organ goes out, the abdomen curls). `enraged` is the last one alone: the thorax flushed crimson, the eye lit, the near wing torn at the tip.",
